{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>Two thousand seven hundred.</b> And it does not say ״and seven hundred״ in the manner it said concerning the sons of Gershon ״and six hundred and thirty״, and concerning the sons of Merari ״and two hundred״, ״and five hundred and eighty״. Perhaps it alluded by the absence of the vav to Korah and those who died with him, who were of the sons of Kohath. Or perhaps it is because the number of the seven hundred is differentiated in gradation from the number of the thousands by reason of the affair of Korah; therefore it did not say ״and seven hundred״ to add on to the first matter and equate them together. And although the Torah publicized only Korah in that affair, it is possible that a branch of Korah's [family] followed him somewhat, or because his brothers and relatives did not protest against him."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:05.886960795Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}